                    "text": "# STAFF AUTHENTICATION SYSTEM \u2014 COMPLETE ARCHITECTURAL AUDIT\n\nHere is the full report. No code has been modified.\n\n---\n\n## 1. REGISTRATION (Sign Up)\n\n**Frontend Files Involved:**\n- `src\/pages\/Staff.tsx` (line ~1-60: imports EmailAuthContext, uses `signUp()`)\n- `src\/hooks\/useEmailAuth.tsx` (lines 151-181: `signUp()` callback)\n- `src\/services\/auth.ts` (lines 55-64: `signUp()` method)\n\n**Flow:**\n```\nStaff.tsx (UI form)\n  \u2192 useEmailAuth().signUp({ email, password, full_name, role, specialization, phone })\n    \u2192 authService.signUp(data)\n      \u2192 POST \/api\/auth\/register.php (via apiClient)\n        \u2192 PHP: register.php\n```\n\n**PHP Backend (`public_html\/api\/auth\/register.php`):**\n- Requires: `email`, `password`, `full_name`\n- Optional: `role` (default: \"doctor\"), `specialization`, `phone`, `bmdc_registration`, `name_bn`\n- Rate limit: `register_{ip}`, 100 req\/60s (default)\n- Password validation: minimum 6 characters\n- Role validation: whitelist of allowed roles\n- **SQL executed:**\n  ```sql\n  INSERT INTO users (email, password_hash, full_name, name_bn, role, specialization, phone, bmdc_registration, is_active, registration_status, email_verified_at)\n  VALUES (:email, :password_hash, :full_name, :name_bn, :role, :specialization, :phone, :bmdc_registration, 1, \"pending\", NULL)\n  ```\n- **Password hashing:** `password_hash($password, PASSWORD_BCRYPT)` \u2014 correct bcrypt\n- **Registration status:** `'pending'` \u2014 requires admin approval\n- **No session created** on registration \u2014 user cannot log in until approved\n- **Duplicate email handling:** If `registration_status = 'rejected'`, re-registration updates the existing record. If any other status, error 409.\n- **Audit log:** `logAudit($userId, null, 'create', 'user', $userId, ...)` inserts into `audit_logs` table\n\n---\n\n## 2. ADMIN APPROVAL\n\n**Frontend Files:**\n- `src\/pages\/Staff.tsx` \u2014 \"Pending Approvals\" tab with list of pending users\n- `src\/hooks\/useEmailAuth.tsx` \u2014 `approveAccount()`, `rejectAccount()`, `getPendingAccounts()`\n- `src\/services\/auth.ts` \u2014 `approveAccount()`, `rejectAccount()`, `getPendingAccounts()`\n- `src\/hooks\/useAdminSave.ts` \u2014 `approveStaffAccount()`, `rejectStaffAccount()` wrappers\n\n**Flow:**\n```\nStaff.tsx (Admin clicks \"Approve\")\n  \u2192 useEmailAuth().approveAccount(userId, role?)\n    \u2192 authService.approveAccount(id, role)\n      \u2192 POST \/api\/auth\/approve.php\n        \u2192 middleware: requireAdmin() \u2014 checks users.role = 'admin'\n          \u2192 PHP: approve.php\n```\n\n**PHP Backend (`public_html\/api\/auth\/approve.php`):**\n- **Authorization:** `requireAdmin()` \u2014 only users with role='admin' can approve\n- **SQL executed:**\n  ```sql\n  UPDATE users SET \n    registration_status = 'approved',\n    approved_by = :approved_by,\n    approved_at = NOW()\n    [, role = :new_role]\n  WHERE id = :id\n  ```\n- **Role assignment:** Optional `role` parameter allows admin to set\/change the role during approval\n- **Rejection:** Same flow via `reject.php`, sets `registration_status = 'rejected'`\n- **Audit logging:** Both approval and rejection logged in `audit_logs`\n\n**UI:** The Staff.tsx page has a \"Pending Approvals\" tab. Admin views pending accounts via `getPendingAccounts()` \u2192 `GET \/api\/auth\/pending.php` (admin-only), then approves\/rejects.\n\n---\n\n## 3. STAFF LOGIN\n\n**Complete flow:**\n\n```\n                      FRONTEND                                         BACKEND\n                      \nStaff.tsx \/ App.tsx (login form \/ Landing page)\n  \u2193\nuseEmailAuth().signIn(email, password)\n  [line 183-199 of useEmailAuth.tsx]\n  \u2193\nauthService.signIn(email, password)\n  [src\/services\/auth.ts:50-52]\n  \u2193\napiClient.post('\/auth\/login.php', { email, password })\n  [src\/lib\/apiClient.ts:145-151]\n  \u2192 fetch() with credentials: 'same-origin'\n  \u2193\nPOST \/api\/auth\/login.php\n  [public_html\/api\/auth\/login.php]\n  \u2193\nhelpers.php: handleCors(), requireMethod('POST')\n  \u2193\ncheckRateLimit('login_{ip}', 5, 900)  \u2190 5 attempts per 15 min\n  \u2193\ngetJsonInput() \u2014 reads php:\/\/input\n  \u2193\nvalidateRequired($input, ['email', 'password'])\n  \u2193\nsanitizeEmail($email) \u2014 FILTER_SANITIZE_EMAIL + FILTER_VALIDATE_EMAIL\n  \u2193\nPDO prepared statement:\n  SELECT id, email, password_hash, full_name, name_bn, role, specialization, \n         phone, photo_url, signature_url, bmdc_registration, is_active, \n         registration_status \n  FROM users WHERE email = :email LIMIT 1\n  \u2193\nValidation pipeline:\n  1. User exists?                          \u2192 401 if not\n  2. is_active = 1?                        \u2192 403 if deactivated\n  3. registration_status = 'approved'?      \u2192 403 if pending\/rejected\n  4. password_verify($password, $hash)?     \u2192 401 if wrong\n  \u2193\nsession_regenerate_id(true) \u2014 prevents session fixation\n  \u2193\ncreateSession($user['id']):\n  - bin2hex(random_bytes(64)) \u2014 128-char hex token\n  - INSERT INTO user_sessions (user_id, token, ip_address, user_agent, expires_at)\n  - SESSION_LIFETIME = 86400 * 7  (7 days)\n  \u2193\nsetcookie('session_token', $token, [\n  'expires' => time() + SESSION_LIFETIME,\n  'path' => '\/',\n  'secure' => true,\n  'httponly' => true,\n  'samesite' => 'Lax',\n]);\n  \u2193\nUPDATE users SET last_login_at = NOW() WHERE id = :id\n  \u2193\nlogAudit(... 'login', ...)\n  \u2193\nResponse: { token, user: { id, email, full_name, role, ... } }\n  \u2193\nBack in useEmailAuth.tsx:\n  setAuthToken(result.token)   \u2190 in-memory only (module-level variable)\n  setCurrentDoctor(result.user) \u2190 React state\n```\n\n**Functions involved:**\n| Layer | Function | File |\n|-------|----------|------|\n| React | `signIn()` | `useEmailAuth.tsx:183-199` |\n| Service | `authService.signIn()` | `services\/auth.ts:50-52` |\n| API Client | `post()` | `lib\/apiClient.ts:145-151` |\n| PHP Entry | login.php | `api\/auth\/login.php` |\n| Auth Check | `getAuthUser()` | `middleware.php:30-109` |\n| Token Extraction | `getBearerToken()` | `middleware.php:272-303` |\n| Session Creation | `createSession()` | `middleware.php:308-328` |\n| Rate Limiting | `checkRateLimit()` | `helpers.php:80-119` |\n| Audit Logging | `logAudit()` | `helpers.php:251-282` |\n\n---\n\n## 4. SESSION STORAGE \u2014 COMPLETE ANALYSIS\n\n### 4a. PHP Session Cookie (`session_token`)\n- **What:** 128-character hex token (64 random bytes)\n- **Where:** Browser cookie, HttpOnly, Secure, SameSite=Lax\n- **Why:** Server-side session identifier; no JavaScript access\n- **Duration:** 7 days (`SESSION_LIFETIME = 86400 * 7`)\n- **Acceptable:** \u2705 YES \u2014 this is the correct approach\n\n### 4b. In-Memory Token (`_authToken`)\n- **What:** The same session token stored in a module-level variable\n- **Where:** `src\/hooks\/useEmailAuth.tsx`, lines 58-71\n- **Why:** Used to attach `Authorization: Bearer` header on API calls (the apiClient sends cookies automatically, so this is **redundant**)\n- **Duration:** Lifetime of the browser tab\/window (lost on refresh)\n- **Acceptable:** \u26a0\ufe0f REDUNDANT \u2014 cookies auto-send with `credentials: 'same-origin'`\n\n### 4c. React Context (`currentDoctor`)\n- **What:** `DoctorAccount` object (`useState<DoctorAccount | null>`)\n- **Where:** `EmailAuthContext` in `useEmailAuth.tsx`\n- **Why:** Provides user info to all components\n- **Duration:** Until tab close or logout\n- **Acceptable:** \u2705 YES \u2014 normal React state\n\n### 4d. PHP Server Session (`user_sessions` table)\n- **What:** Session record: token, user_id, ip_address, user_agent, expires_at, last_activity\n- **Where:** MySQL `user_sessions` table\n- **Why:** Server-side session validation and expiry\n- **Duration:** 7 days, then cleaned up by `cleanupExpiredSessions()`\n- **Acceptable:** \u2705 YES\n\n### 4e. What is NOT stored (correctly):\n- \u274c **No localStorage for auth tokens** \u2014 migration complete\n- \u274c **No sessionStorage** \u2014 not used\n- \u274c **No IndexedDB** \u2014 not used for auth\n- \u274c **No Cache API** \u2014 SW caches static assets only, not auth data\n- \u274c **No Service Worker** \u2014 SW does not cache API responses for auth\n\n---\n\n## 5. CROSS-DEVICE LOGIN\n\n**Status: \u2705 Works across devices and browsers.**\n\n**Why it works:**\n1. **Token is stored server-side** in `user_sessions` table\n2. **Cookie is set with domain=''** (current domain only) \u2014 works on any device\n3. **Session token sent via cookie OR Authorization header** \u2014 flexible transport\n4. **No device-specific localStorage** \u2014 nothing ties a session to a specific device\n\n**Flow on new device:**\n```\nUser goes to drarmankabir.com\n  \u2192 No session cookie \u2192 App shows login form\n  \u2192 User enters credentials \u2192 POST \/api\/auth\/login.php\n  \u2192 Server creates session \u2192 Sets HttpOnly cookie\n  \u2192 Cookie stored in new device's browser\n  \u2192 All subsequent requests include cookie\n```\n\n**Session restore works because:** The cookie is sent with every request; `verifySession()` on the server checks the `user_sessions` table. If the token exists and hasn't expired, the session is valid.\n\n**Limitations:** No concurrent session limit \u2014 a user can be logged in on unlimited devices simultaneously. Sessions are not invalidated on other devices when logging in elsewhere (no \"kick other sessions\" feature).\n\n---\n\n## 6. SESSION RESTORE (Page Refresh)\n\n**Complete flow:**\n```\nBrowser refresh \/ app load\n  \u2193\nEmailAuthProvider mounts (useEmailAuth.tsx:127)\n  \u2193\nuseEffect \u2192 restoreSession() (lines 135-149)\n  \u2193\nauthService.verifySession()\n  [services\/auth.ts:40-47]\n  \u2193\nGET \/api\/auth\/verify.php\n  [cookies auto-sent with request]\n  \u2193\nmiddleware: getBearerToken() extracts from:\n  1. Authorization: Bearer header (not set for page load \u2014 no JS storage)\n  2. X-Session-Token header (not set)\n  3. session_token cookie \u2190 THIS is used on page refresh\n  \u2193\ngetAuthUser() checks user_sessions WHERE token = :token AND expires_at > NOW()\n  \u2193\nIf valid:\n  \u2192 Returns user data\n  \u2192 setCurrentDoctor(user) \u2190 React state restored\n  \u2192 isInitializing = false\nIf invalid\/expired:\n  \u2192 Returns 401\n  \u2192 currentDoctor stays null\n  \u2192 isInitializing = false\n  \u2192 Login form shown\n```\n\n**What happens if token expires:**\n- Server checks `WHERE expires_at > NOW()` \u2014 expired tokens return null\n- `getAuthUser()` returns null \u2192 `requireAuth()` sends 401\n- `verifySession()` catches the error \u2192 returns null\n- User sees login form, must re-authenticate\n\n**What happens after browser restart:**\n- If the `session_token` cookie is still valid (within 7 days), the browser sends it\n- `verifySession()` succeeds \u2192 user is logged in immediately\n- If the cookie was cleared (browser cleanup, private browsing), user must log in again\n\n**Important:** The in-memory `_authToken` is LOST on page refresh, but this is fine because the cookie is still present and sent with requests. The apiClient uses `credentials: 'same-origin'` which auto-sends cookies.\n\n---\n\n## 7. LOGOUT\n\n**Complete flow:**\n```\nFRONTEND                           BACKEND\n  \u2193\nuseEmailAuth().signOut()\n  [line 201-206]\n  \u2193\nauthService.signOut()\n  [services\/auth.ts:67-73]\n  \u2193\nPOST \/api\/auth\/logout.php\n  [cookies auto-sent]\n  \u2193\nmiddleware: requireAuth()\n  \u2192 getBearerToken() from cookie\/header\n  \u2192 getAuthUser() validates session\n  \u2193\ndestroySession($token):\n  1. DELETE FROM user_sessions WHERE token = :token\n  2. DELETE FROM patient_sessions WHERE token = :token\n  3. DELETE FROM admin_sessions WHERE token = :token\n  4. setcookie('session_token', '', expires=1, ...) \u2190 clears cookie\n  5. unset($_COOKIE['session_token'])\n  \u2193\nlogAudit(... 'logout', ...)\n  \u2193\nResponse: success\n  \u2193\nBack in frontend:\n  clearAuthToken()     \u2190 clears in-memory _authToken\n  setCurrentDoctor(null) \u2190 clears React state\n  setAuthError(null)\n```\n\n**What is cleaned:**\n| Storage Location | What is removed | How |\n|-----------------|----------------|-----|\n| Server DB | `user_sessions` row | `DELETE` |\n| Browser cookie | `session_token` | `setcookie()` with past expiry |\n| In-memory JS | `_authToken` | Set to `null` |\n| React state | `currentDoctor` | `setState(null)` |\n| localStorage | Nothing | No auth data stored there |\n\n---\n\n## 8. REMAINING BROWSER STORAGE REFERENCES\n\n### Search Results: **NONE FOUND**\n\nAfter searching:\n- `source_build\/...\/src\/**\/*.ts` \u2014 **zero** `localStorage` references\n- `source_build\/...\/src\/**\/*.tsx` \u2014 **zero** `localStorage` references\n- `public_html\/**\/*.php` \u2014 **zero** `localStorage` references\n- `public_html\/**\/*.js` (dist) \u2014 **zero** `localStorage` references\n- `storage.getItem` \/ `storage.setItem` \u2014 **zero** direct calls\n\nThe **Storage Adapter Guard** (`src\/lib\/storageAdapter.ts`) is in place with a hard block for business data keys. It allows only UI preference keys:\n```typescript\nconst ALLOWED_UI_KEYS = new Set([\n  'patient_language', 'sidebar_collapsed', 'theme',\n  'table_page_size', 'table_compact_view',\n  'classroom_arman', 'classroom_samia',\n  'chamber_arman', 'chamber_samia',\n  'profile_arman', 'profile_samia',\n  'prescriptionHeaders_chamber', 'prescriptionHeaders_hospital',\n  'app_current_user_email',\n]);\n```\n\nHowever, the `Staff.tsx` page still imports `storage` from `storageAdapter` (line 8). A grep for actual calls to use it returned no results, suggesting the import may be a leftover.\n\nThe pre-existing `STORAGE_AUDIT_REPORT.md` (found in `src\/`) documents ~80+ previously-used keys \u2014 all